This repository requires an adversarial Codex review pass before any pull request
merges. Its presence is read by Gate 2B of ~/.claude/hooks/pre-merge-require-review.sh,
which treats every PR in a repo shipping this file as high-risk: a merge is denied
unless clean findings exist at
~/.claude/codex-findings/<owner>-<repo>/<pr>.json.

Why this file exists rather than relying on the harness-path heuristic:

Gate 2B already escalates any PR that changes a file under .claude/, .github/ or
_Automations/. Every AEC source PR regenerates .github/admission/v1/source-declaration.json,
so in principle every AEC PR was already escalated. That is a coincidence, not a
decision: it depends on where a generated artifact happens to live. Move the
declaration, or land a PR that does not regenerate it, and the review requirement
disappears with no announcement.

This file makes the requirement a declaration instead. It is the same reasoning the
admission protocol applies to source: a property that matters should be stated and
checked, not inferred from an incidental fact about the tree.

To run the belt:  /codex:review  then  /jwCodexIngest
To bypass once:   prefix the merge with SKIP_CODEX_GATE=1 (a WARN is recorded)

Removing this file removes the requirement, which is the point — the decision is
visible in the diff and reviewable like any other change.
